          %h3#as_a_grand_unified_gauge_group As a grand unified gauge group
          %p
            Discussion as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/grand+unified+theory"} grand unified theory
            (see
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "GUT#TheGUTKnownAsSO10"} there
          %ul
            %li#BLM09
              Stefano Bertolini, Luca Di Luzio,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michal+Malinsk%C3%BD"} Michal Malinský
              = succeed "," do
                %em Intermediate mass scales in the non-supersymmetric SO(10) grand unification: a reappraisal
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0903.4049"} arXiv:0903.4049
          %p review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Howard+Georgi"}> Howard Georgi
                , §24 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie Algebras In Particle Physics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429499210"} doi:10.1201/9780429499210
            %li#Malinsky09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michal+Malinsk%C3%BD"}> Michal Malinský
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em 35 years of GUTs - where do we stand?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mpi-hd.mpg.de/lin/seminar_theory/talks/Malinsky.pdf"} pdf
            %li#BaezHuerta10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"} John Baez
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The algebra of grand unified theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.1556"} arxiv:0904.1556
          %p
            for non-superymmetric
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28physics%29"} models
          %ul
            %li#LavouraWolfenstein10
              %p
                L. Lavoura and Lincoln Wolfenstein,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Resuscitation of minimal
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SO
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 10
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(10)
                    grand unification
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.48.264"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.48.264
            %li#AltarelliMeloni13
              %p
                Guido Altarelli, Davide Meloni,
                %em
                  A non Supersymmetric SO(10) Grand Unified Model for All the Physics below
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi GUT
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{GUT}
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1305.1001"}> arXiv:1305.1001
                )
            %li#DueckRodejohann13
              %p
                Alexander Dueck, Werner Rodejohann,
                %em
                  Fits to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SO
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 10
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(10)
                  Grand Unified Models
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.4468"}> arXiv:1306.4468
                )
            %li#FongMeloni14
              %p
                Chee Sheng Fong, Davide Meloni, Aurora Meroni, Enrico Nardi,
                %em
                  Leptogenesis in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SO
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 10
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(10)
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1412.4776"}> arXiv:1412.4776
                )
              %p
                (in view of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leptogenesis"} leptogenesis
            %li#OhlssonPernow19
              %p
                Tommy Ohlsson, Marcus Pernow,
                %em Fits to Non-Supersymmetric SO(10) Models with Type I and II Seesaw Mechanisms Using Renormalization Group Evolution
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.08241"}> arXiv:1903.08241
                )
            %li#CPS19
              %p
                Mainak Chakraborty, M.K. Parida, Biswonath Sahoo,
                %em Triplet Leptogenesis, Type-II Seesaw Dominance, Intrinsic Dark Matter, Vacuum Stability and Proton Decay in Minimal SO(10) Breakings
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.05601"}> arXiv:1906.05601
                )
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Results indicating non-SUSY
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SO
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 10
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(10)
                  as self sufficient theory for neutrino masses, baryon asymmetry, dark matter, vacuum stability of SM scalar potential, origin of three gauge forces, and observed proton stability.
            %li
              %p
                Nobuchika Okada, Digesh Raut, Qaisar Shafi,
                %em
                  Inflation, Proton Decay, and Higgs-Portal Dark Matter in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SO
